 them to the successful king Sugrīva, Vibhîşana and other Rākşasas and monkeys by whose help he had achieved victory.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.219,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-39-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7038011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c487c18b90dab0252dba4227a57b78e61a08f55e34508316bb5ee23c2ce52bb","compact":"c2fc07c8e6b5b3826f651d655bc87a0330c7b19b11e43a3f032029c5a4fdc54b","nasal":"c2fc07c8e6b5b3826f651d655bc87a0330c7b19b11e43a3f032029c5a4fdc54b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-38-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":38,"verse":12,"english":"Next morning Råma, being present in the sacrificial ground and having sent for the Rşis, Vasiştha,-Vamadeva Jābāli, Kasyapa, Visvämitra, carrying on penances for a long time, Durvāsā, Pulastya of hard austerities, Śakti, Bhargava, Markandeya living long, the highly illustrious Maudgalya, Gargya, Gargya, Cyavana, Śatānanda, conversant with religions, effulgent Bharadvaja, Agni's son Vasuprava, Narada, Parvata, the great Gautama and other ascetics of firm vows, assembled with minds possessed by curiosity. The highly powerful Räkșasas and monkeys also came there out of curiosity.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.193,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-96-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7038012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"44178ade13e406e81805fef3db00212874922f126dcf6b220047b6d594721e34","compact":"3c9e6da19acdd6ba0558abdfc8970f6824da95817d2a72efe653deac2338b6dc","nasal":"3c9e6da19acdd6ba0558abdfc8970f6824da95817d2a72efe653deac2338b6dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-38-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":38,"verse":13,"english":"And those highly powerful monkeys and night-rangers wore on their heads and arms those jewels conferred on them by Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.217,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-39-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7038013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"22597c7d0d5e5c7dc2f1b4e32640cc06b84d9b5845f6d8ae0d95f90f7e4dfaa4","compact":"55dda9e82f8aee9271b25dff45d8a6be991258ef378364d2c1eb276d045ec429","nasal":"55dda9e82f8aee9271b25dff45d8a6be991258ef378364d2c1eb276d045ec429"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-38-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":38,"verse":14,"english":"The monkeys lived there all happily feasting on fragrant honey, well-cooked meat and various fruits and roots.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.3,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-39-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7038014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"222e3a13b2de684688897ed6141b9bceba63bf2ba094aec50ed21d3968539cba","compact":"ed80d494525cc12f0b32412e7ed8c4a016eb8413320d8b9a378972541e1cf5c3","nasal":"ea42c9896e4cb8e958d5d13e223fb77bb7730bb78d7959233ece9551bef5ab60"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-38-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":38,"verse":15,"english":"In this way they spent more than a month—but it appeared to them as a moment on account of their devotion to Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.459,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-39-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7038015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a58f558d023dd57b0c867d2e5d2d773ae81189b345354de48ffbf7dc2a992389","compact":"edf1884df0b53f5751ba3c59f03af0dd87049da8470a21b3499a354910798527","nasal":"edf1884df0b53f5751ba3c59f03af0dd87049da8470a21b3499a354910798527"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-38-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":38,"verse":16,"english":"He, too also spent his time happily with monkeys assuming shapes at will, the highly powerful Rakşasas and the mighty bears.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.328,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-39-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7038016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"75f6dfb5715450ffd0e5d7610d93eba4eee308c8612ef13b8af9cce040993d9c","compact":"cae3beadd5121771eed3ffa94a16ff2dcb97cce45bffdcec4a04b6e9380f0be0","nasal":"cae3beadd5121771eed3ffa94a16ff2dcb97cce45bffdcec4a04b6e9380f0be0"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-38-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":38,"verse":17,"english":"In this way, the delighted monkeys and Rāks asas spent the second winter month. Enjoying delight they thus spent their days happily in the city of Ayodhyā working to the welfare of Rama.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-39-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7038017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6dfe4617ece0f101cb086d21ee29b015bac2a6fb1d77617cdaeb156c814b676a","compact":"7900473087d0bc10d52d67b76cfb979580fdcfa236e0874ad211a0a74bead153","nasal":"7900473087d0bc10d52d67b76cfb979580fdcfa236e0874ad211a0a74bead153"}}]
